  "markdown_content": "## Incident Details\\n\\nRegional authorities in Russia's south reported that air attacks they attributed to Ukrainian forces killed two people and wounded 17 others.\\n\\nLocal officials said emergency responders were dispatched to multiple sites following the strikes. Hospitals in the affected areas received dozens of people for treatment, with authorities reporting that 17 people sustained a range of injuries. Two fatalities were confirmed by regional authorities, who said investigations were underway to document the damage and casualties.\\n\\n## Location and Context\\n\\nOfficials provided limited immediate detail on exactly where the strikes occurred, saying only that the attacks hit sites in southern districts close to the international border. For now, authorities have described the incident as part of continuing cross-border escalations and have appealed to residents in border areas to follow emergency guidance.\\n\\nThe reported strikes come amid an extended period of fighting and repeated cross-border incidents, which both Moscow and Kyiv have publicly blamed on the other side at different times. International observers and humanitarian groups have repeatedly warned that civilian populations in border regions remain at risk from such attacks.\\n\\n## Casualties and Response\\n\\n- 2 fatalities confirmed by regional authorities\\n- 17 people reported injured, treated at local hospitals\\n- Emergency responders dispatched to multiple sites\\n- Dozens of people received medical attention at hospitals\\n\\n## Verification and Next Steps\\n\\nAt the time of publication, there was no independent verification of the claims and no immediate comment from Ukrainian officials. Local authorities said they would release further details as emergency teams complete assessments and as investigations progress.",
